cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it as below."
title: "the-world: a deterministic spherical digital-life simulation platform"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic spherical digital-life simulation platform with a Python engine and a
  Rust/PyO3 numerical core. The project investigated whether signal use and other behavioural
  structure could arise under selection without an explicit fitness function or an LLM in the
  simulation loop. It closed on 2026-10-24; end-to-end emergence was not established, while
  mechanism-layer results, negative results, and a reusable methodology are documented.
authors:
  - name: "the-world contributors"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fish827-08/the-world"
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - digital life
  - agent-based simulation
  - spherical grid
  - evolution
  - reproducibility
